{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Retrieval queries for the starter corpus. Replace and EXTEND these with the lookups you actually make: the point is to encode your real questions, then notice when a corpus change makes one stop resolving. Never edit an expectation to turn a run green \u2014 that converts the only honest signal here into decoration. `mode: any` passes when an expected memory lands in the top 3; `none` asserts a query finds NOTHING, which is how false positives get caught.",
